<title>RUSSIA: Uneximbank says to bid for a share of Rosneft oil firm.</title>
<headline>Uneximbank says to bid for a share of Rosneft oil firm.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's third largest bank Uneximbank is considering bidding for a stake in state-owned oil company Rosneft, the last oil company still fully owned by the state, Uneximbank President Vladimir Potanin said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Uneximbank was part of the winning consortium for 25 percent plus one share of telecom holding company Svyazinvest, and is taking part in the tender of a controlling stake in mining giant Norilsk Nickel, which it is widely backed to win.</p>
</text>
